cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or pipeline in research, please cite it as follows."
title: "FinDroid-BD 400: Android FinTech and Financial Malware Research Dataset"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, real-data research dataset of 311 validated Android apps spanning 147 benign
  fintech applications (crypto wallets, mobile-money/PSP wallets, bank-retail fintech, and
  fintech-utility apps from F-Droid official builds) and 164 real Android banking-trojan samples
  (Cerberus, Alien, ERMAC, Hook, Coper, CopyBara, Octo, Anatsa/TeaBot, Crocodilus, ExobotV2,
  Godfather, Vultur, ToxicPanda/TgToxic) sourced from the public MalwareBazaar research repository.
  Each sample carries a verified SHA-256, validated APK, fintech/family labels, 66 static-extracted
  feature columns, and full provenance. Built for cybersecurity education and Android malware
  analysis research.
type: dataset
